# Feature architecture (normative)

**Before implementing or refactoring anything under `apps/webapp`, read:**

[`docs/specs/feature-architecture-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/feature-architecture-spec.md)

## Must follow

1. **Classify the entity** — complex (URL drawer) · simple (row `···` only) · thin drawer · layout variant.
2. **Toolbar** — `[Primary CTA] [Search] [Main filter <select>] [Filter] [More]`; no chip-bar main filters.
3. **Locked routes** — assessments at `/evaluations` (all `kind`s); no `/homework` nav; no `/configuration/roles`; no resource UI in v1.
4. **Staff permissions** — Catalog at `/configuration/permission-profiles`; grant rows on Staff drawer → Permissions (`staffPermissionAssignments`); see spec **§5.3.1**; not a roles matrix screen.
5. **Class attendance** — `attendanceMode` on class config; `/attendance` nav only when `daily`; daily = list of days + drawer.
6. **Incidents** — resolve via **`resolveIncidentWithOutcomes`** in one modal; involved students read-only in drawer.
7. **Assessments** — one drawer; exclusive body section by `kind`; homework is `kind = homework` on evaluations.
8. **Do not** invent parallel routes or drawers for simple entities (Fee, Payment, GradeScale, DisciplinaryAction).

## Agent checklist (every screen)

- [ ] Route matches §6 route index
- [ ] Surface type matches entity (§3): complex · simple · thin · layout
- [ ] Locked UX decisions respected (§4)
- [ ] No resource UI, `/configuration/roles`, or `/homework` nav
